MTS patch: no baby for a mother on cooldown, and a readiness file for the
agents (setting mtsNoCooldownBypass, default 0 = stock). Applies after
time-scale.patch and turn-clock.patch (patches go in name order).

The birth cooldown is already on the game clock: server.cpp's Time:: is
MTSGameTime (time-scale.patch), so birthCoolDown = Time::timeSec() + the
stock Kumaraswamy sample (0..300, mean ~2 min) is game seconds, frozen
while the turn clock holds, and player saves shift it with the other game
timestamps. What let babies come fast is the stock fallback: when every
fertile mom is on cooldown the mother search runs again ignoring cooldowns.
With mtsNoCooldownBypass=1 that retry keeps the cooldown, so with no mom
ready the login gets the stock no-mother outcome (a new Eve). To let the
agents avoid that, the server writes mtsBirthReady.txt in the run dir,
"<readyCount> <soonestCooldownEndGameSeconds>" (fertile, not cursed, off
cooldown, below maxLivingChildrenPerMother and the early-birth cap, in a
place she may have babies; soonest = 0 if none on cooldown), checked every
0.5 wall s and written on change and at least every 3 s.

